-- Image-scan seed data for local dev / playground.
--
-- Snapshots a handful of IMAGE_SCAN jobs pulled from a live cluster so
-- the new detail page renders with realistic vulns / labels / signatures
-- / secrets without operators needing to spin up a real scanner pod.
--
-- Contents:
--   4 image_digests spanning public + private registries
--   4 IMAGE_SCAN jobs (all SUCCEEDED) with different vuln profiles:
--     - ghcr.io/dexidp/dex           — 177 vulns (shows paging + HIGH density)
--     - quay.io/metallb/controller   —  33 vulns (mid-size)
--     - git.torden.tech/.../homelab  —   8 vulns (small, realistic)
--     - git.torden.tech/.../spam-operator — 0 vulns (clean image)
--   Matching image_scan_runs + image_scan_artifacts (labels + cosign + secrets)
--   Top 40 vulns per scan by severity.
--
-- Skips the big blobs (full grype.json, full sbom.json) to keep the
-- seed file under ~100KB. The parsed image_vuln_findings rows contain
-- what the UI actually needs; raw downloads point at an artifact that's
-- intentionally empty in the seed.
--
-- Regenerate with the psql script in docs/regenerate-image-scan-seed.md
-- (or re-run the block in the feat/job-kubernetes-scanner PR discussion).

BEGIN;

